1. Modules

Program is categorise into three main components:
1.1 main.c
1.2 OledMenuGui.c and .h
1.3 Spin asm presets

1.1 main.c

Its file commonly use to combine everything within flash folder and its not different here.
But there are few aspects that I will differentiate:
- variables and typedefs -

- pwm setups - pwm setup is crucial with that circuit because if you will look up FV1 documentation
you will see that potentiometers interface is directly connected to DSP core. Since we dont use analog
controls such as potentiometers but rather pwm with LP filter our core will be expose to noise much more than
with typical application. For that matter we reduced resolution from 10bit to 8bit, it's a bit paradoxical
because lower resolutions tends to have more jitter noise, yet our prescaler one will have higher carrier frequency
that is much higher than carrier frequency for 10bit and acoustic range frequency's.

- encoder and button logic - algorithms like our encoder logic are commonly known as state machines, we
constatly checking wich state are we in. There are many state which create this machine so to control this
easily we use typedef enum

